## The ONE metric (FROZEN — revised only as a declared epoch, never edited in place)
`{{PRIMARY_METRIC}}` = {{METRIC_DEFINITION}}. {{PRIMARY_DIRECTION}} = better. Computed by
`{{FROZEN_SCORER_PATH}}` (FROZEN). You change what FEEDS the metric, never how it is computed — unless
the metric itself is found wrong, which is a **metric epoch** (`roles/worker.md` §Metric epochs): a new
`metric_version`, a verified kill of the old metric (or, for a scorer that did not compute this
specification, the check that reproduces the discrepancy), this section updated, and the retained
contenders re-scored. The epoch record is `configs/loop.json` `campaign.metric_epochs` — the block is
absent until the first revision; with no block, the current `metric_version` is the co-designed first
epoch, ratified, and it never needs an entry of its own; who may open one is `campaign.metric_revision`,
the user's dial. **Epoch, not fork:** when
the ruler was wrong but the save-sets are valid and re-scorable, open an epoch and the ledger survives;
when the artifacts themselves are tainted (a forward-model bug, corrupted data), that is
`fork-campaign` — a clean break with a fresh ledger.
- **Hard bounds:** {{METRIC_HARD_BOUNDS}}.
- **Plausible a-priori range:** {{METRIC_PLAUSIBLE_RANGE}}. Predict before you run. A result outside
  this range is a red flag to investigate, not a triumph. What the spend gate accepts as a prediction is
  `configs/loop.json` `campaign.prediction_mode`, set once at setup; this campaign is
  `{{PREDICTION_MODE}}`. Never weaken it to get past an awkward prediction: a fabricated range is a fake
  control, and so is a mode picked for convenience.
- **Baseline (exp 000):** {{BASELINE_DESCRIPTION}} → the floor to beat. Measure it; don't assume it.
  Also keep the **trivial/degenerate reference** scores (all-zeros / constant / mean / a trivial physical
  state): a result that loses to a trivial answer is not a win, and a non-physical trivial answer that
  wins flags a metric/units error (`{{VERIFY_SKILL}}` checks this per claim).
